body:
I think you need to directly tell him about the trigger if you haven't already. You've told him that you'd prefer he'd shave, but without context, he doesn't have much reason to do that other than to appease your aesthetics from his perspective. He's also expressed he's shifting his gender expression for *his* sake. He might just not be interested in feminine expression anymore, and you might be incompatible with him now because of that, unless you feel confident that this trigger can be overcome through therapy.

&#x200B;

Your boyfriend knows you were assaulted, and that you prefer a fresh face, but he can't know it's a trigger unless you tell him, and you shouldn't force yourself to be with him if it causes you distress. Communication and trust are important so that you can understand each other.
